## Current evidence

The Ant result is **{{effect}} m/s world-Y velocity {{ci}}** on {{n}} original confirmation pairs, with {{retention}}% mean forward-speed retention. Its recorded status remains `{{status}}`; both arms have {{baseline_failures}}/{{n}} failures and a shared pre-onset ending violates the strict prefix rule. The later audit reproduces {{fresh_effect}} m/s {{fresh_ci}} on {{fresh_n}} separate resets, with failures increasing from {{fresh_baseline_failures}} to {{fresh_failures}}. These cohorts must not be pooled or assigned the same failure-rate conclusion.

The random-direction comparison rank is {{random_p}}, and lateral-label specificity is not supported. Projection ablations and an observation transformation support heading involvement, but the transformation rotates already-clipped contact channels. Exact physical-heading equivalence and unique mediation are unestablished. The audit consumed a previously reserved application cohort; the new cohort guard prevents its reuse.

{{rank_qualification}}

The [current Ant findings](ant-classic-005-findings.md), [independent audit](ant-classic-005-independent-audit.md), [paper](paper.md), and [interactive explorer]({{site}}) are generated from pinned evidence. The [completion ledger](../docs/ant-publication.md) records corrections, historical noncompliance, and remaining limits. Earlier [rigor](scientific-rigor-audit.md), [specificity](ant-classic-005-y-shift-audit.md), and [path-mechanism](ant-classic-005-mechanism-audit.md) reports retain their historical analyses; the current findings supersede stronger semantic claims. HalfCheetah's negative outcomes remain below.
